{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This is a wrong-face-of-the-venue case, not an in-radius arrival. The driver's own trace never brings him closer than 284.95 m to the VivoCity pin — outside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius of POL-NS-02 — but he is stationary at that point across the waiting window and therefore inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling, which is exactly the case POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-02 route to POL-NS-03 rather than to the geofence test. The trace is IMPAIRED at weight 0.8, issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median 18 s sampling against a 10 s nominal cadence); I disclose that, and it does not touch a minimum-distance figure, which is unaffected by sample spacing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00206", "EV-TRIP-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "The dwell limb of POL-NS-03 is met. The driver's arrival is recorded at 15:12:05 and the trip is terminated at 15:18:40 — a 6.6 minute wait (trip_record.wait_time_min 6.6, about 395 seconds) — against the free waiting period of 300 seconds in force for this trip (platform_policy.free_wait_sec). The trace records him stationary at 0.0 km/h at the 285 m point, so the required continuous dwell is satisfied on the GPS clock and not merely on a button tap; the trace is impaired at weight 0.8 (LOW_SAMPLE_RATE) and I disclose it, but the stationary window is the one fact the prepass found established beyond argument.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00206", "EV-GPS-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "The mislocation is pin ambiguity, and pin ambiguity is charged to the platform, not to this driver. The chat log carries two SYSTEM notifications and nothing else — 'Driver assigned. Meet at VivoCity, Lobby L.' and 'Your driver has arrived' — and not one message from either party naming a block, entrance, tower or bay over the waiting window. The pickup zone has four registered pickup points (trip_record.registered_pickup_points = 4). Under POL-NS-03(ii), where neither party specified a sub-location and registered_pickup_points is 2 or more, the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the $4.00 cancellation fee — SGD 2.00 — charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00206", "EV-TRIP-00206", "EV-FARE-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.goodwill",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider here and cannot strip the driver of his compensation. Limb (a) requires the chat log to show that the RIDER sent at least one locating or coordinating message during the waiting window; the log holds two SYSTEM messages and nothing from the rider, so limb (a) fails on the face of the artifact and POL-NS-04 is not engaged. The case therefore falls to be decided under POL-NS-03, which is the clause that carries the driver's goodwill.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is not false, and no false-arrival finding may be recorded against this driver. POL-NS-05 catches a marker only where the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin, or moving at 15 km/h or more, at the marker. The driver's minimum distance across the entire trace is 284.95 m — inside the 300 m line — and he was stationary, not in motion, so neither trigger fires. POL-NS-05's own closing words route a driver stationary within 300 m of the pin but outside the arrival radius to POL-NS-03. (Trace impaired at weight 0.8, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, disclosed.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00206", "EV-TRIP-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "The LOW_SAMPLE_RATE tag does not impair this trace for policy purposes, and nothing on this record escalates. POL-NS-08(b) is met only by a sampling gap longer than 120 s inside the waiting window, fewer than 6 fixes across that window, or an omitted rider_track. The trace reports max_gap_sec 0.0 with an empty gaps array, 52 driver fixes, and a populated rider track of 31 fixes, so no limb of POL-NS-08(a) to (d) fires. The prepass tag is schema-level only: per POL-GEN-02 I disclose it and it down-weights confidence, but it does not engage the escalation route in POL-NS-09(e).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.driver_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    },
    {
      "text": "No anti-farming inference may be drawn against this driver, so there is no basis to withhold his payment. On POL-NS-07's check the profile shows driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d of 1 — below the threshold of 4 — and 1 against driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 187, a rate of 0.005 against the 0.08 threshold, so neither limb is met and these fields cannot support an adverse finding. No other profile field is relied on; POL-GEN-01 confines these two counters to this test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's refund and the driver's payment are not in competition, and the shortfall route cannot swallow the wrong-entrance route. The driver's stationary fixes never enter the arrival geofence, so POL-NS-06's in-geofence dwell arithmetic has no purchase here; POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-02 both expressly route a driver stationary outside the radius but within 400 m of the pin to POL-NS-03, which fixes both the rider's full refund of the $4.00 and the driver's platform-funded SGD 2.00 goodwill. Under POL-GEN-03 the two figures are independent and are never netted. (Trace cited here is impaired at weight 0.8, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, disclosed; the trip, chat and fare artifacts are all at weight 1.0.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00206", "EV-TRIP-00206", "EV-FARE-00206"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.8
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 2.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver — this decision is issued without human review; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04.\n\nFINDING. The driver did not reach the pickup point. His own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00206) never brings him closer than 284.95 m to the VivoCity Lobby L pin and returns 0 qualifying in-radius fixes; he waited at the HarbourFront kerb across the road, held position there for about 395 s (the trip record's 6.6-minute wait), and cancelled at 15:18:40 under reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. The rider's track in the same trace places the rider at the pin (mean 15.43 m from it).\n\nOUTCOME. The $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and the driver receives a $2.00 platform-funded goodwill payment.\n\nWHY THE FEE FALLS. Under POL-NS-02 a driver is deemed arrived only on at least three consecutive fixes, each at 25 m accuracy or better, inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius; there are none, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. POL-NS-01 limb (d) fails too: the trip was terminated under DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which that limb does not recognise and which the clause treats as the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider. Because the driver's stationary position (284.95 m) lies outside the arrival radius but inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling, and the dwell exceeded the 300 s free waiting period in force, POL-NS-03 governs and refunds the fee in full. The driver's own statement — that the map put him at the HarbourFront kerb — says the same thing; it carries no weight multiplier, but it agrees with the instrument evidence.\n\nWHY THE DRIVER IS STILL PAID. Neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00206 holds two SYSTEM notifications and no party message), and the pickup zone has 4 registered pickup points (EV-TRIP-00206). POL-NS-03(ii) therefore attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity and pays the driver 50% of the $4.00 fee = $2.00, funded by the platform and never recovered from the rider. Under POL-GEN-03 the $4.00 refund and the $2.00 goodwill are independent and are never netted. The monetary effect is $6.00, below the $8.00 automatic-execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes on issue.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHT (POL-GEN-02). EV-GPS-00206 carries the deciding position fact and is impaired at weight 0.8 (issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, median 18 s cadence against a 10 s nominal). The discount is disclosed and does not disturb the finding: the impairment concerns sample spacing, not position, and a 285 m miss is far outside any sampling or accuracy effect. The artifact is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08 (largest gap 0.0 s, 52 driver fixes, rider track present), so no PARTIAL_REFUND ceiling and no POL-NS-09(e) escalation engages. Confidence is capped at the trace's 0.8, above the 0.70 floor. EV-ADVIS-00206-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and carries no fact; its absence is why POL-NS-06(i) interval-summing is unavailable, and nothing here needs it. No referral is produced: POL-NS-05 does not fire (the marker is not false), and the POL-NS-01 reason-code referral applies only where the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, which is not this case.\n\nCLAIMS. Driver claims on the wrong-face position, the 285 m/400 m ceiling, the 6.6-minute dwell against the 300 s free waiting period, and the $2.00 pin-ambiguity goodwill are accepted and they decide the case. The driver's point that POL-NS-04 is not engaged is accepted (the rider sent no locating message, so limb (a) fails), and the rider's own track does not change the outcome. The driver's point that the arrival marker is not false is accepted: 284.95 m is inside POL-NS-05's 300 m line and he was stationary, so no false-arrival referral is recorded and POL-NS-03 governs. The driver's POL-NS-08 and escalation points are accepted. The driver's anti-farming point is accepted (no_show_terminations_30d 1, rate 0.005, both below POL-NS-07's thresholds), but POL-NS-07's 80% payout ($3.20) is not the payment here: POL-NS-03 displaces the no-show route, so the driver's payment is the $2.00 goodwill, not $3.20. Rider claims that POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (d) fail, that this is the POL-NS-03 fact pattern, that fault allocation under POL-NS-03(ii) keeps the cost off the rider, that the LOW_SAMPLE_RATE tag is schema-level only and does not engage the partial-refund ceiling, and that confidence sits at 0.8 above the floor are all accepted. The rider's separate point that he was present at the pin is accepted as fact, but POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate him because limb (a) requires a rider message and there is none — the full refund comes from POL-NS-03, not POL-NS-04. The rider's alternative POL-NS-06 shortfall route was discarded at the mechanical stage for citing the absent advisory artifact without naming its issue code; it is not relied on and would in any event reach the same refund."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Even on the narrowest reading - treating this as a waiting-period shortfall rather than a wrong-location case - the fee is still refunded in full. The effective in-geofence dwell computed under POL-NS-02 is 0.0 seconds, against the 300 s free waiting period in force and a stated shortfall of 300.0 seconds, so POL-NS-06 makes the cancellation fee not chargeable and refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present. Limb (i) cannot rescue the fee either: EV-ADVIS-00206-01 is MISSING, so there is no traffic_advisory present and populated to permit separate intervals to be summed, and limb (ii) confirms an advisory never excuses a shortfall in any event. (The trace is IMPAIRED, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, weight 0.8.)",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00206-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

