    "explanation": "Rider and driver, this dispute is decided as follows.\n\nTHE FEE. The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged to the rider is refunded in full.\n\nWHY. Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if all four of its limbs hold. Limb (b) fails: the driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00206) never places him inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius around the VivoCity pin - his closest approach across the whole trace is 284.95 m, and the arrival test returns zero qualifying in-radius fixes (POL-NS-02). Limb (d) fails: the trip record records the trip terminated under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01(d) states in terms that this code is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy the limb. The fee is therefore not chargeable.\n\nTHE GOVERNING CLAUSE. The driver was stationary for the required dwell (trip_record.wait_time_min 6.6, about 395 s) at a point outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pickup pin (284.95 m), against the 300 s free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). POL-NS-03 makes the 400 m ceiling the whole test, and on these facts the driver did not arrive at the pickup point, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the fee is refunded to the rider in full - SGD 4.00.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S PAYMENT. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00206) holds two SYSTEM notifications and no message from either party naming an entrance, block, tower or bay, and the pickup zone has four registered pickup points (registered_pickup_points = 4). Under POL-NS-03(ii) the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 per cent of the SGD 4.00 fee - SGD 2.00 - charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. Per POL-GEN-03 the rider's refund and the driver's payment are independent and are never netted against each other.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. The driver's claims that this is a wrong-face-of-the-venue case decided under POL-NS-03, that his stationary wait met the required dwell, that the mislocation is pin ambiguity, that POL-NS-04 is not engaged, that POL-NS-05's false-arrival trigger does not fire, and that POL-NS-06's in-geofence shortfall arithmetic has no purchase because his fixes never entered the geofence, are accepted and lead to the same outcome. On POL-NS-05: the closest approach is 284.95 m, inside the 300 m line, and he was stationary at the marker rather than travelling at 15 km/h or above, so the arrival marker is not false and no false-arrival referral is recorded. The driver's POL-NS-07 point (no anti-farming pattern: no_show_terminations_30d = 1 against completed_trips_30d = 187, a rate of 0.005) is accepted as far as it goes, but POL-NS-07 does not fix his payout here: POL-NS-01 is not satisfied and POL-NS-03 displaces it, so the SGD 2.00 is the POL-NS-03(ii) platform goodwill, not the 80 per cent compensation of POL-NS-07. The rider's claims that POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (d) fail, that POL-NS-03 requires a full refund, that the goodwill is platform-funded and never recovered from the rider, and that the GPS impairment is schema-level only, are accepted. The rider's POL-NS-04 claim is accepted only in part: the rider track (31 fixes, mean 15.43 m, maximum 22.50 m from the pin) shows the rider stood at the app-dropped pickup point, but POL-NS-04 does not apply because its limb (a) requires a locating message sent by the rider in the chat log and there is none.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHT AND CONFIDENCE. The deciding position fact rests on EV-GPS-00206, weight 0.8, issue code LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median 18 s sampling against a 10 s nominal cadence). I name the artifact, its weight and its issue code: the finding survives the discount, because 52 fixes at 100 per cent coverage with a largest interval of 26 s cannot move a stationary position 285 m. The tag is schema-level only - it meets no limb of POL-NS-08(a) to (d) (no gap, well over 6 fixes, rider track present) - so it neither caps the ruling at a partial refund nor engages escalation under POL-NS-09(e); it caps confidence under POL-GEN-02(2) at the artifact's 0.8, which is above the platform-wide 0.70 floor. The bundle mean is context only and is not the cap. The rider's waiting-period-shortfall claim under POL-NS-06 was discarded at the mechanical check for citing the MISSING advisory EV-ADVIS-00206-01 without naming its issue code, and it is not reinstated; POL-NS-06 is not the route to this refund.\n\nESCALATION AND EXECUTION. No escalation: confidence is 0.80, at or above the 0.70 floor; there are no repeat no-show disputes between these parties (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0); and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip. The monetary effect is SGD 6.00 (SGD 4.00 refund plus SGD 2.00 goodwill), below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling executes automatically."
  },
