    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this was a pin-ambiguity pickup at a large venue. The $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and the driver receives a separate platform-funded goodwill payment of $2.00. The two figures are independent and are not offset.\n\nWhat the record shows. The booking's pickup pin is VivoCity, Level 1, Lobby L (1.2644, 103.8221), a LARGE_VENUE zone. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00206) never brings him closer than 284.95 m to that pin, and his recorded speed there is 0.0 km/h. The trip was accepted 15:03:30, his 'arrived' marker is 15:12:05, and he terminated the trip at 15:18:40 under reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, a wait the trip record (EV-TRIP-00206) measures at 6.6 minutes against the 300-second free waiting period in force.\n\nThe charge does not stand. POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails: a stationary position 284.95 m from the pin is outside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, so POL-NS-02 does not deem the driver arrived. Limb (d) fails independently: DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own statement that he could not find the rider, and it is not one of the three reason codes limb (d) recognises. The $4.00 fee (EV-FARE-00206; platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd $4.00) is therefore refunded to the rider in full.\n\nThe route is POL-NS-03. Because the driver's stationary fixes lie outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, POL-NS-03 governs. Neither party named a block, entrance, tower or bay - the chat log (EV-CHAT-00206) holds only two SYSTEM notifications - and the venue has 4 registered pickup points, so the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party. The driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50% of the $4.00 fee, i.e. SGD 2.00 (EV-FARE-00206 money block). It is charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-04 claim is accepted as to presence but does not exonerate the rider. The rider's position is well established - 31 fixes, mean 15.43 m and maximum 22.50 m from the pin, inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius. But POL-NS-04 limb (a) requires the chat log to show a locating message sent by the rider, and the log contains no rider message at all. POL-NS-04 therefore does not apply and does not strip the driver's goodwill; the refund does not depend on it.\n\nNo false-arrival referral. POL-NS-05 catches the marker only where the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin, or moving at 15 km/h or more, at the marker. The driver was 284.95 m away and stationary, so neither trigger fires and no false-arrival record is entered. Nor is there a reason-code education referral: POL-NS-01 directs that only where the stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, which they do not.\n\nEvidence weight and confidence. EV-GPS-00206 is impaired at weight 0.8, issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median 18 s sampling against a 10 s nominal cadence). That is disclosed, and the finding survives the discount: coverage is 100% across 52 driver fixes, the largest interval is 26 s, the gaps list is empty, so none of POL-NS-08's own limbs (a) to (d) is met and neither the PARTIAL_REFUND ceiling nor POL-NS-09(e) is engaged; a 285 m miss is far beyond any sampling or accuracy error. The deciding position fact rests on EV-GPS-00206, so confidence is capped at 0.80, above the platform's 0.70 floor; the case is decided here rather than sent to human review. EV-TRIP-00206, EV-CHAT-00206 and EV-FARE-00206 all carry weight 1.0. No POL-NS-09 trigger is open: the profiles' counterparty-dispute counts are 0, rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming counters are 1 of 187, far below both limbs.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-06 waiting-period-shortfall claim was discarded by the referee: it cited the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00206-01 (weight 0.0) without naming its issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. It is not needed, because POL-NS-03 already produces the full refund.\n\nExecution. The monetary effect is $4.00 + $2.00 = $6.00, below the $8.00 automatic-execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so this provisional ruling executes on issue unless either party appeals under POL-GEN-04."
  },
